      "side": 1,
      "message": "The key has 7 args and the value has 10 args.\n\n- base function approach may have many dup default args\nmakeKey(arg1, arg2) {\n    return makeKey(arg1, arg2, arg3Default, arg4Default, arg5Default, \n    arg6Default, arg7Default);\n}\nmakeKey(arg1, arg3) {\n    return makeKey(arg1, arg3Default, arg3, arg4Default, arg5Default, \n    arg6Default, arg7Default);\n}\nmakeKey(arg1) {\n    return makeKey(arg1, arg2Default, arg3Default, arg4Default, \n    arg5Default, arg6Default, arg7Default);\n}\nmakeKey(arg1, arg2, arg3, arg4, arg5, arg6, arg7) {\n    return new key(arg1, arg2, arg3, arg4, arg5, arg6, arg7)\n}\n\n- renaming build helper may be hard for mutli-arg\nmakeKey\u0027WithArg2\u0027(arg1, arg2) { \u003c- actually arg1 and arg2 are both changing. \u0027\u0027\n    return new key(arg1, arg2, arg3Default)\n}\n\n\nHow about builder? Or any new arg change in test key/value, we may need a new build helper which has many duped default values because key/value needs many arg in ctor.\n\nHere is a comparison for builder v.s. helper\n\n// Downstream4Key\n// Use builder\nUpstream4Key keyTcp \u003d new Upstream4Key()\n    .setProto(IPPROTO_TCP)\n    .build();\n\nUpstream4Key keyDownstreamA \u003d new Upstream4Key()\n    .setDownstreamIfindex(downstreamIfindex)\n    .setDownstreamMac(downstreamMac)\n    .setPrivateAddr(privateAddr)\n    .setPrivatePort(privatePort)\n    .build();\n\n// Current required helper function (l.1360, l.1780)\n@NonNull\nprivate Tether4Key makeUpstream4Key(int proto) {\n    if (proto !\u003d IPPROTO_TCP \u0026\u0026 proto !\u003d IPPROTO_UDP) {\n        fail(\"Not support protocol \" + proto);\n    }\n    return new Tether4Key(DOWNSTREAM_IFINDEX, DOWNSTREAM_MAC, (short) proto,\n        PRIVATE_ADDR.getAddress(), REMOTE_ADDR.getAddress(), PRIVATE_PORT, REMOTE_PORT);\n}\n\n@NonNull\nprivate static Tether4Key makeUpstream4Key(final int downstreamIfindex,\n        @NonNull final MacAddress downstreamMac, @NonNull final Inet4Address privateAddr,\n        final short privatePort) {\n    return new Tether4Key(downstreamIfindex, downstreamMac, (short) IPPROTO_TCP,\n        privateAddr.getAddress(), REMOTE_ADDR.getAddress(), privatePort, REMOTE_PORT);\n}\n\n\n// Downstream4Key\n// Use builder\nDownstream4Key keyDefault \u003d new Downstream4Key()\n    .build();\n\nDownstream4Key keyUdp \u003d new Downstream4Key()\n    .setProto(IPPROTO_UDP)\n    .build();\n\nUpstream4Key keyDownstreamA \u003d new Downstream4Key()\n    .setPublicPort(publicPort)\n    .build();\n\n\n// Current required helper function (l.1374, l.1401, l.1788)\n@NonNull\nprivate Tether4Key makeDownstream4Key() {\n    return makeDownstream4Key(IPPROTO_TCP);\n}\n\n@NonNull\nprivate Tether4Key makeDownstream4Key(int proto) {\n    if (proto !\u003d IPPROTO_TCP \u0026\u0026 proto !\u003d IPPROTO_UDP) {\n        fail(\"Not support protocol \" + proto);\n    }\n    return new Tether4Key(UPSTREAM_IFINDEX,\n            MacAddress.ALL_ZEROS_ADDRESS /* dstMac (rawip) */, (short) proto,\n            REMOTE_ADDR.getAddress(), PUBLIC_ADDR.getAddress(), REMOTE_PORT, PUBLIC_PORT);\n}\n\n@NonNull\nprivate static Tether4Key makeDownstream4Key(final short publicPort) {\n    return new Tether4Key(UPSTREAM_IFINDEX, MacAddress.ALL_ZEROS_ADDRESS /* dstMac (rawip) */,\n            (short) IPPROTO_TCP, REMOTE_ADDR.getAddress(), PUBLIC_ADDR.getAddress(),\n            REMOTE_PORT, publicPort);\n}",
